            "text": "RTB · 2A DAILY INTEL · Tuesday, July 28, 2026",
            "spacing": "None"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Large",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "text": "Fifth Circuit reopens the constitutional foundation of federal gun control — and civilian suppressors leave the military export system",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "text": "On July 20 the Fifth Circuit voted to rehear U.S. v. Squire en banc — not as a Second Amendment case but as a Commerce Clause challenge to the federal felon-in-possession ban, following Justice Thomas's Hemani concurrence. Separately, two interim final rules move suppressor exports from State/ITAR to Commerce, effective Nov 20.",
            "wrap": true,
            "spacing": "Small"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Small",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "color": "Warning",
            "text": "HOTTEST LEADS",
            "spacing": "Medium"
          },
          {
            "type": "FactSet",
            "facts": [
              {
                "title": "1. Fifth Circuit takes Squire en banc (Commerce Clause)",
                "value": "Heat 88 ▲▲"
              },
              {
                "title": "2. Suppressor exports move State → Commerce",
                "value": "Heat 87 ▲▲▲"
              },
              {
                "title": "3. New Jersey T-3 to the July 31 effective date",
                "value": "Heat 84 ▲▲"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Small",
            "weight": "Bolder",
            "color": "Warning",
            "text": "WHAT'S MOVING",
            "spacing": "Medium"
          },
          {
            "type": "TextBlock",
            "size": "Small",
            "text": "• 5th Cir. grants en banc in U.S. v. Squire — Higginson dissents, no argument date\n• Suppressors off the Munitions List — most provisions effective Nov 20, 2026\n• New Jersey T-3 — AG dealer/owner guidance still unposted\n• Colorado T-4 — DOR covered-firearms list still unpublished",
            "wrap": true
          }
        ],
